{
  "duration": 76.759,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.14,
      "end": 1.719,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.399,
      "end": 3.439,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.0,
      "end": 4.92,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.339,
      "end": 6.159,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.719,
      "end": 7.519,
      "text": "two trains"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.94,
      "end": 9.34,
      "text": "start from two cities"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.92,
      "end": 12.319,
      "text": "which are four hundred twenty kilometers apart."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.96,
      "end": 15.279,
      "text": "One train is moving at sixty kilometers per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.899,
      "end": 16.699,
      "text": "and the other train"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.219,
      "end": 19.42,
      "text": "is moving at eighty kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.039,
      "end": 27.719,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find after how many hours the two trains will meet. Now, the important point here is that both trains are moving towards each other,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.42,
      "end": 34.319,
      "text": "so the distance between them is getting reduced from both sides at the combined rate of their speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.819,
      "end": 37.059,
      "text": "Therefore, when two bodies move towards each other,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.639,
      "end": 40.219,
      "text": "their relative speed is the sum of their speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.68,
      "end": 46.739,
      "text": "Relative speed equals sixty plus eighty equals one hundred forty kilometers per hour. Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.34,
      "end": 48.579,
      "text": "Now we have everything we need."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.139,
      "end": 53.119,
      "text": "We know distance equals four hundred twenty kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.579,
      "end": 58.759,
      "text": "Relative speed equals one hundred forty kilometers per hour. Now we can use the speed-distance-time formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.279,
      "end": 62.779,
      "text": "Time equals distance divided by relative speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.319,
      "end": 64.599,
      "text": "Substituting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.0,
      "end": 68.299,
      "text": "time equals four hundred twenty divided by one hundred forty."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.019,
      "end": 70.099,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.5,
      "end": 71.4,
      "text": "we get three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.22,
      "end": 76.759,
      "text": "So the trains will meet after three hours. Hence, the correct option is option B."
    }
  ],
